    "title": "Darrien Miller helps Biloxi Shuckers secure 5-1 win over Biscuits",
    "text": "On Tuesday, June 23, at 7:35 p.m., Darrien Miller, a former Clovis West High School standout, contributed to the Biloxi Shuckers’ 5-1 victory over the Montgomery Biscuits in their MiLB matchup.\nThe contest was held at DABOS Park. This marked the 13th game between the teams this season, with the Shuckers now leading the season series 7-6 against the Biscuits.\nMiller tallied 3 hits in 4 at-bats, scored 1 run, notched 1 RBI and stranded 1 runner.\nThe Shuckers are set to face the Biscuits again on Wednesday, June 24, at DABOS Park.",
    "summary": "On Tuesday, June 23, at 7:35 p.m., Darrien Miller, a former Clovis West High School standout, contributed to the Biloxi Shuckers’ 5-1 victory over the Montgomery Biscuits in their MiLB matchup. The contest was held at DABOS Park. This marked the 13th game between the teams this season, with the Shuckers now leading the season series 7-6 against the Biscuits. Miller tallied 3 hits in 4 at-bats, scored 1 run, notched 1 RBI and stranded 1 runner. The Shuckers are set to face the Biscuits again on Wednesday, June 24, at DABOS Park.",
